NewMod legal and packaging review — 2026-11-21

This is an engineering inventory, not legal advice or a declaration of
license compliance. NewMod is derived from No Quarter by the No Quarter Mod
Team and its contributors, with selected Jaymod/Oz-inspired behavior and
other third-party components. See PROVENANCE.md and CHANGES. Review the actual
license texts, their interaction, and all notices before deploying or
redistributing the source, binaries, or a server package.

Retained texts and notices
--------------------------
* licenses/NoQuarter-LICENSE.txt — exact source license text from the NQ
  snapshot (Modified Reciprocal Public License, modified by the NQ team).
* licenses/NoQuarter-media-readme.txt — NQ's asset notice and credits.
* licenses/Jaymod-LICENSE.txt and licenses/Apache-2.0.txt — Jaymod's Apache
  notice and the full Apache 2.0 text. Jaymod also requires the original id
  terms, credit and bundling both licenses; see its upstream README.
* licenses/id-ET-SDK-License.rtf and licenses/ETPub-id-ET-SDK-License.rtf —
  the id SDK license texts retained from the inspected Jaymod and Oz trees.
* licenses/Lua-5.1.txt — Lua.org/PUC-Rio permission notice, also in lua.h.
* licenses/SHA1-Paul-E-Jones.txt and src/sha-1/license.txt — the SHA-1
  implementation's notice.
* src/cgame/md5.h and src/cgame/md5.c — RSA Data Security, Inc. MD5 notice
  and Colin Plumb implementation notice, respectively. The optional key
  code uses a seeded MD5 derivative. Similar inherited headers and notices
  occur elsewhere; do not strip them.
* Omnibot/ contains NQ's Omni-Bot interface headers/loader. Determine and
  retain any additional upstream notices and terms for the interface and a
  separately supplied bot library; they have not been fully reviewed here.

Known separate asset restriction
--------------------------------
The NQ asset notice states: "Use of files WITHIN No Quarter pk3s is prohibited
without consent." Its notice attributes original content to the No Quarter
mod team (2005–2011) and suggests contacting the NQ community. Contact the
rights holders and obtain appropriate permission before using or redistributing
those files. Necessary base-game data, maps, models, sounds and textures also
have their own rights/terms. No NQ pk3 or other game media is included here;
the local synthetic server fixture was for testing only and is not a playable
asset package. Permission to use source does not itself clear the media.

Outstanding deployment/distribution conditions
-----------------------------------------------
* The NQ license describes reciprocal source availability, a distinct name,
  dated/attributed modification records both in source and CHANGES, retained
  notices, and notification of the licensor (section 6 contains details and
  time limits). It also includes a restriction against removing checks or
  manipulating the product to run on older ET versions such as 2.55. Preserve
  those checks and review the exact language. The inherited server/client
  engine-version checks have not been removed.
* The supplied NQ license refers to an EXHIBIT A notice but the retained
  upstream license text does not itself contain an EXHIBIT A section. Identify
  the intended notice and ensure all file-level notice and change-location
  cross-reference requirements are met before distributing. Existing comments
  and CHANGES are an engineering record, not a legal-compliance certification.
* Provide a durable, complete source download and future updates as required,
  including build inputs and required components; notify the NQ licensor or
  use the alternative notice method specified in the license if direct notice
  is impossible. No publication or notification is represented as completed.
* Resolve whether the NQ reciprocal terms, Jaymod's Apache 2.0 notice,
  original id SDK terms, Lua terms, Omni-Bot terms and any asset conditions
  are compatible for the intended distribution. Request permissions or
  further legal review where needed; do not assume one license supersedes the
  others. Retain the unmodified upstream license texts and copyrights.
* Choose an authorized and technically validated packaging method for both
  server and client modules and necessary media. This repository is not a
  complete distributable/playable mod package.
